ject's references, a ctypes class's StgInfo's."] [88 4 "// CType_Type_traverse: proto, argtypes, converters, restype, checker, pointer_type (the argument lists'"] [89 4 "// arrays may be a base's too, PyCStgInfo_clone's copy: left visible to Go)"] [98 1 "// cyHideC is ExtCyHide: the handles C holds only from within the probed set, and the probed classes' StgInfos, out"] [99 1 "// of their tables until the returned function puts them back (by node index: no object kept)."] [142 14 "// a reference C holds from outside the set"] [175 1 "// cyClearC is ExtCyClear: the trash's C-born objects' tp_clear (delete_garbage), its classes' StgInfos dropped."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[32 56] [82 22] [87 21] [114 12] [114 19] [124 22] [141 23] [148 29]]} (go/file "cycles.go" :imports [

    ;; The C world's objects in pyi's cycle collector (queue 609; py's finalize.go, ExtCyIsNode, ExtCyTraverse, ExtCyHide,
    ;; ExtCyClear), ported from CPython 3.14.10's Modules/gcmodule.c's design and Modules/_ctypes/_ctypes.c's
    ;; CType_Type_traverse and CType_Type_clear (the PSF's license, LICENSE.md):
    ;;
    ;;   - A C-born object (cObj) is a node. Its references are its Go value's (outer, its managed dict) and those its type's
    ;;     tp_traverse visits, run in the world with a visitproc of pyi's (_Pyi_gc_visit) that records each handle.
    ;;   - Before a probe, a handle whose every C reference (its ob_refcnt) the probed objects' tp_traverse accounts for is
    ;;     taken out of the handles' maps (and its mirror's, its variable-size proxy's): the references C holds inside the
    ;;     set, as gc's subtract_refs finds them; a handle with a reference more is held from outside, as in CPython.
    ;;   - A class with a StgInfo (ctypes' metatypes' classes) lists its StgInfo's references (proto, __pointer_type__,
    ;;     restype, errcheck), and the StgInfo table (stgs, CPython's type object itself) lets go of a probed class.
    ;;   - The final trash's C-born objects get their tp_clear (delete_garbage), in a C entry whose end releases the handles
    ;;     they no longer hold; a dead class's StgInfo is dropped (CType_Type_clear).


